namespace trion:
    use software

    section "The trion command":
        The trion command means the command that runs the trion processor.
        The trion verify command means the subcommand of the trion command that verifies a package.
        The trion doc command means the subcommand of the trion command that writes a document of a package.
        The trion lsp command means the subcommand of the trion command that serves an editor.
        A diagnostic means a message that the trion command reports about a package.
        The severity of a diagnostic is error, warning, or information.
        A gate means a step of the trion verify command.
        The state of a gate is passed, failed, or skipped.
        A verified package means a package that has no failed gate.
        Each package has one or more readings.

        [TOOL-VERIFY]
        When an author runs the trion verify command on a package P,
        the trion verify command shall follow this flow:
            step check: check the statements of P;
            step sources: check the sources of P;
            step prover: decide the queries of P with the external prover;
            step properties: check the readings of P;
            step stability: decide P at raised bounds;

            start check
            check -> sources
            sources -> prover
            prover -> properties
            properties -> stability
            finish stability

        [TOOL-EXIT]
        If a gate of a package is failed, then the trion verify command shall fail.

        [TOOL-DOC-VERIFIED]
        The trion doc command shall write a document of a verified package only.

        [TOOL-LSP]
        The trion lsp command shall report the diagnostics of each open source file to the editor.
